'' fbc's OWN fbc-int/query-symbol.bas, with its suite runner, RUN. Three things kept it from
'' running: TKO0770 on the reserved name it queries; the reserved class answered 0; and,
'' in this Debug build, an abort in StmtCall_ (latesweeps4.bas), which took a STATEMENT
'' payload for every node and read past 'stmts' -- out of bounds once the index met the
'' vector's capacity. 355 of its 357 asserts pass; the two that do not ask for
'' FB_SYMBCLASS_KEYWORD of 'integer' (line 84) and FB_SYMBCLASS_FWDREF (line 116), which
'' are not answered yet -- and are why the runner exits 1.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target win64-msvc -m fbc-tests tests/vendor/fbc-tests/fbc-tests.bas tests/vendor/fbc-tests/fbc-int/query-symbol.bas -o tests/codegen/qsymvendor.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/win64-msvc
'' ENV: TKO_INCLUDE=toolchains/tiko-windows/inc
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-NOT: TKO0770
'' RUN: tests/codegen/qsymvendor.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:      357       355         2  fbc_tests.fbc_int.query_symbol                 3
